### Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The bug report indicates that the Lighthouse audit is incorrectly suggesting the use of `preconnect` or `dns-prefetch` for domains that are already being preconnected. The images show that `preconnect` is already used for `https://www.google-analytics.com` and `https://fonts.gstatic.com`, yet the audit still suggests adding them.

The root cause of this issue is likely that the audit does not check the DOM for existing `link rel=preconnect` or `dns-prefetch` tags before making its suggestions. This results in false positives where the audit suggests optimizations that are already implemented.

### Bug Location and Fix

The bug is located in the `lighthouse-core/audits/uses-rel-preconnect.js` file. The audit logic needs to be updated to check for existing `preconnect` or `dns-prefetch` links in the DOM.

